[Chapter "Against ...c5"]
[Line "The exchange 4...cxd4"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{Black's best answer to 3...c5 lines: exchange in the centre.} 1. d4 {Start with the queen's pawn.} 1... d5 2. Nc3 {The Jobava idea: the knight comes to c3 before the c-pawn moves, ready for Nb5 or e4.} 2... Nf6 3. Bf4 {Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before e3.} 3... c5 4. e3 {Support d4.} 4... cxd4 5. exd4 {Recapture towards the centre. The e-file opens and the bishop gets d3.} 5... a6 {Black takes b5 away from the knight.} 6. Nf3 {Develop and control e5.} 6... Nc6 7. Ne5 {The knight takes up a strong central post and supports a kingside attack.} *
